**How to implement.** Red first for 001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash' (.spec-md §3.3): every seeded entry id, and every minted source id, is the canonical string of a GUID. Facts only; no production file changes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs`, beside the seeded-sources facts: (a) `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal`: for every entry of `seedEntries`, `Guid.TryParse e.entryId.value` succeeds (matched, never `.IsSome`) and the parsed GUID's `string` equals `e.entryId.value`, the lowercase hyphenated form `SampleId.toElementValueId` writes (`ElementId.fs:43`); and the ids are distinct. The samples pass; it fails today on the presets' text ids. (b) `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`: two `newSourceId ()` calls each parse as a GUID whose `string` equals the id, and the two differ. It fails today on the `src-` prefix (`ElementId.fs:594`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs`, `Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id` (`:144-149`): its name and its first two assertions stay; `Assert.StartsWith("source-add:src-", calls.[0])` becomes: `calls.[0]` starts with `source-add:` and the rest is the canonical string of a GUID. It fails today.

**Acceptance.** After the facts land, constructor-unit-tests (SourceLibraryTests) MUST fail with exactly `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal` and `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`, every other SourceLibraryTests fact passing; ui-tests (LightSourceEditorTests) MUST fail with exactly `Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id`, every other LightSourceEditorTests fact passing; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.
